※ pl4g-test: compile=ok opt=0,1 run=native,qemu exit=0 diag=none

※ An arena given back in every arm that reaches the join is given back, so a pure function that
※ empties its arena in both arms of an `if` has given it back on every way out.

fn both(c: bool) → bool:
    let s: mut arena = ⎕arena
    let t: str = "a" ⧺ "b" in s
    let r: bool = t = "ab"
    if c:
        ⎕empty(s)
    else:
        ⎕empty(s)
    r
@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    if both(true): 0u6 else: 1u6
